  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection and Promotion of Human Rights of Persons with Albinism in Mozambique: Maputo, Nampula, Zamb&#xe9;zia and Tete, 2021-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM is a partner implementing the project with UNESCO as the lead agency. The project seeks to enhance access to and availability of health, protection and juridical services for people with albinism through capacity building of relevant actors. IOM&apos;s role will be to strengthen the capacity of key stakeholders (health-workers, law enforcement officers, community leaders and media professionals on issues related to human rights international standards and mechanisms against persons with albinism and gender approach to albinism.</narrative>
  </description>
